          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21234 misc: keep delayed work off isolated CPUs",
        "message": "LU-21234 misc: keep delayed work off isolated CPUs\n\nDelayed work queued without naming a CPU runs where its\ntimer expired, and on Linux 6.9 to 6.18 that can be an\nisolated CPU held by a realtime task, which leaves the work\na few percent of that CPU. DNE lock cancels wait for the\ndelayed object free, so service threads stalled for minutes.\n\nQueue such work on unbound workqueues, which stay off\nisolated CPUs, or on a named CPU where kfilnd wants one.\nUse system_dfl_wq, or system_unbound_wq on older kernels.\nAlso give the first ldlm pool recalc delay in jiffies.\n\nFixes: 444d29c21891 (\"LU-18938 obdclass: delay an object free\")\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity,sanity-sec\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I63ae4ccbde52edda7d60d482c0397199e4a6134e\n"
      },
